{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdVkPkeUns1PHXsgx3W5k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_015EUsVoVQrbjy55rbY86xFU","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/var/folders/XX/XXXX/T/skilleval-golden-01-1-fxk_z0ao/.eval-home/.claude/projects/-private-var-folders-g9--dhv-jzj5ljd5nywv14y31hm0000gn-T-skilleval-golden-01-1-fxk-z0ao/memory/feedback_worktree_jam.md","content":"---\nname: worktree_jam_fix\ndescription: Procedure to unstick a jammed git worktree — prevents expensive rediscovery\nmetadata:\n  type: feedback\n---\n\nWhen a git worktree is jammed (git status hangs or fails to complete), use this procedure:\n\n1. Run `git status` to see what is held/blocking\n2. Find the `index.lock` file (usually in `.git/` directory)\n3. Identify the PID that owns it (via `lsof index.lock` or `ps aux`)\n4. Kill that PID: `kill -9 <pid>`\n5. Prune the stale worktree entry: `git worktree prune`\n\n**Why:** This specific sequence has resolved worktree jams repeatedly this week. Agents rediscovering it from scratch each session is expensive.\n\n**How to apply:** If an agent encounters a hung or failing git operation on a worktree (especially index.lock contention), apply this procedure before trying other diagnostics or suggesting more complex fixes.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6918,"cache_read_input_tokens":17536,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6918},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"REDACTED","uuid":"4a99fb78-b8d1-4f6f-ae45-643aefc2c38b","timestamp":"2026-07-29T04:52:20.563Z","request_id":"req_011CdVkPjzYRinTWFywPC1st"}
